{"authored" [{"question" "q-125457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{1}{y}\\,i-\\frac{1}{x}\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ Interpret circulation as the sum of four convergent improper line integrals over the open quadrant arcs, with independent one-sided limits at $(\\pm1,0)$ and $(0,\\pm1)$. The field is undefined at those four points, so the original ordinary circulation is not defined." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125457/review.json" "file_sha256" "a101f083dcb4ea1c94976a5b59096d2d503a5d01534f5cc886f80aa7ee1b6c68" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125457/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "ba7dee03d238a03f6d7f46fc653ac1c0be8aba3c4fda8f9e0d6314cedd5d2a10" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125457/verification.json" "basis" 1938 "rationale" "Supply the omitted convergent improper-integral convention. Four independently convergent quadrant integrals yield -4pi; ordinary original circulation remains undefined."} {"question" "q-125457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The original field is undefined at the four axis intersections, so an ordinary line integral over the whole circle is not defined. For the explicit improper interpretation, $r(t)=(\\cos t,\\sin t)$ traverses the unit circle counterclockwise. On each open quadrant arc,\n\n$$\\frac{1}{y}\\,dx=\\frac{-\\sin t}{\\sin t}\\,dt=-dt,\\qquad-\\frac{1}{x}\\,dy=\\frac{-\\cos t}{\\cos t}\\,dt=-dt.$$\n\nThus the scalar pullback is $-2$. Each endpoint has the finite one-sided limit $-2$, so each open-arc integral converges absolutely and equals $-\\pi$. Their sum is $\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{imp}}=-4\\pi$, the unchanged option a. No principal-value cancellation is used, and $F$ remains undefined at the excluded points." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125457/review.json" "file_sha256" "a101f083dcb4ea1c94976a5b59096d2d503a5d01534f5cc886f80aa7ee1b6c68" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125457/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "ba7dee03d238a03f6d7f46fc653ac1c0be8aba3c4fda8f9e0d6314cedd5d2a10" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125457/verification.json" "basis" 1938 "rationale" "Supply the omitted convergent improper-integral convention. Four independently convergent quadrant integrals yield -4pi; ordinary original circulation remains undefined."} {"question" "q-125457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4\\pi "] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125457/review.json" "file_sha256" "a101f083dcb4ea1c94976a5b59096d2d503a5d01534f5cc886f80aa7ee1b6c68" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125457/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "ba7dee03d238a03f6d7f46fc653ac1c0be8aba3c4fda8f9e0d6314cedd5d2a10" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-125457/verification.json" "basis" 1938 "rationale" "Supply the omitted convergent improper-integral convention. Four independently convergent quadrant integrals yield -4pi; ordinary original circulation remains undefined."} {"question" "q-125457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{1}{y}\\,i-\\frac{1}{x}\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b9b5f54f71142e3b519c67634b4b8eb18028b59d5a77e955f28f5b94598f30c" "basis" 1936 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{y}\\,i-\\frac{1}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-2(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =-4\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b9b5f54f71142e3b519c67634b4b8eb18028b59d5a77e955f28f5b94598f30c" "basis" 1936 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0739c96ad346238c47110cc19d8571d34c4c37477e99709f7d89249005e6827" "basis" 1936 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b9b5f54f71142e3b519c67634b4b8eb18028b59d5a77e955f28f5b94598f30c" "basis" 1936 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-15\\pi "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b9b5f54f71142e3b519c67634b4b8eb18028b59d5a77e955f28f5b94598f30c" "basis" 1936 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060266/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "val